{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-instanton-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:categorical-instanton-exists","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of existence of categorical instantons","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-instanton-exists"],"cites":["references/belavin-polyakov-schwartz-tyupkin1975"],"text":"categorical-instanton-exists-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:categorical-instanton-exists\"></a><p>The trivial connection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_0 = d</code> has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_{\\nabla_0} = 0</code>, which\nis by definition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star_q</code>-self-dual; hence the zero instanton exists.\nNon-trivial instantons exist on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code>-bundles over the\nCR realisation (<a href=\"#ex:c-quantum-observable-universe\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/qou-examples\">example</a>) via\ncategorical <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-descent\">descent</a> of the classical instanton of A. A. Belavin, A. M. Polyakov, A. S. Schwartz, and Yu. S. Tyupkin (BPST) <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"belavin-polyakov-schwartz-tyupkin1975\">[belavin-polyakov-schwartz-tyupkin1975]</span>\n(self-duality, proved below).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-instanton-exists-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-categorical-instanton-exists","qa":{"counts":{"pass":56,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":59},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
